{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">People rate a good-looking interface as easier to use even when the actual functionality is identical to a plain one — this is a documented bias, the aesthetic-usability effect, not a coincidence.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Visual polish buys real goodwill and forgiveness for minor friction, but it doesn't change the underlying interaction cost — a redesign can win on sentiment while task-completion metrics stay flat.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Track perception (sentiment, surveys) and task performance (completion rate, error rate) as two separate signals, and weight objective task metrics over subjective ratings when a redesign's glowing feedback doesn't match its funnel numbers.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
